This directory has short example scripts for pair_style uma (ML-UMA).

UMA model weights are NOT shipped with LAMMPS (FAIR Chemistry License).
Export a FP64 TorchScript artifact from a user-supplied FairChem checkpoint
before running. pair_coeff names that artifact directory. One MPI rank and
several MPI ranks need different exports.

Single rank (one GPU, or CPU LibTorch)
  Writes model_traced.pt + metadata.json in the output directory.

  PYTHONPATH=src/ML-UMA/uma-engine/python python \
    src/ML-UMA/uma-engine/python/export_artifact.py \
    --checkpoint $UMA_CHECKPOINT --dtype float64 --task omat \
    --output /path/to/uma-s-1p2-omat-f64

  lmp -in in.nacl.nvt -var uma_art /path/to/uma-s-1p2-omat-f64
  lmp -in in.nacl.npt -var uma_art /path/to/uma-s-1p2-omat-f64

Graph-parallel (one MPI rank per GPU, devices 1)
  Each rank loads OUT/w{W}/r{R}/. Export W times with EXPORT_WORLD=W.
  N_LIST is the rocksalt repeat of this example (3x3x3 -> 216 atoms).
  Changing the atom count requires a new export.

  ENG=src/ML-UMA/uma-engine
  export PYTHONPATH=$ENG/python TRACE_DEV=cuda N_LIST=3
  export EXPORT_WORLD=2 OUT=/path/to/uma-s-1p2-omat-f64-w2
  for R in 0 1; do
    EXPORT_RANK=$R python $ENG/python/export_blocks_xpu.py
  done

  mpiexec -n 2 lmp -in in.nacl.npt -var uma_art /path/to/uma-s-1p2-omat-f64-w2

  pair_coeff names the parent directory (the one that contains w2/), not
  an individual r{R} folder. Do not pass a single-rank export_artifact.py
  directory to mpiexec -n W; the ranks will not find w{W}/r{R}.

in.nacl.nvt
  NaCl rocksalt 3x3x3 (216 atoms), 10-step NVT at 300 K.
  pair_style uma precision double, newton off.

in.nacl.npt
  Same crystal, 10-step NPT. virial auto (the default) enables the
  strain-gradient virial when the barostat is present; ac must stay off.

Do not launch with -k on or -sf kk. There is no uma/kk style.

No log.* files are included: the example cannot run in default LAMMPS CI
without LibTorch and a user artifact.
